1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:04,322
GlarePilot: weather and sun glare where — and when — you’ll actually drive

2
00:00:04,322 --> 00:00:08,942
Two modes: Real-data planning (live route
+ forecast) and Manual demo scenarios

3
00:00:08,943 --> 00:00:12,737
Real-data planning: Amherst → Chicago, leaving 8:00 AM tomorrow

4
00:00:12,737 --> 00:00:17,848
Live route + forecast retrieved now — each
point evaluated at its projected arrival time

5
00:00:17,848 --> 00:00:22,378
Trip summary (live data): 14h 24m drive, arrive 9:24 PM CDT

6
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:35,260
Map: route colored by sun glare, with
condition icons at forecast trouble spots

7
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:42,802
Assumed +1 h delay — your assumption, not
traffic data — every later point re-timed

8
00:00:42,802 --> 00:00:46,931
“When should I leave?” — same route, departures
−3 h…+3 h, transparent exposure score

9
00:00:46,931 --> 00:00:52,049
Lower bars = less glare, wet, wind and
after-dark exposure; the best option is marked

10
00:00:52,049 --> 00:00:58,745
Manual demo scenarios — hand-set synthetic data, no weather/route API calls

11
00:00:58,745 --> 00:01:12,449
“Delay shifts the weather” (synthetic): an assumed
75 min delay pushes arrival into rain and dark

12
00:01:12,449 --> 00:01:24,681
“Heavy rain + crosswind” (synthetic): rain and wind
icons where the hand-set squall hits the route

13
00:01:24,681 --> 00:01:30,418
“Westbound sunset glare” (synthetic) — now the 3D chase preview

14
00:01:30,418 --> 00:01:36,243
3D chase preview — simulated playback of the planned route, not GPS

15
00:01:36,243 --> 00:01:42,335
Scroll to look ahead along the route —
HUD: “Previewing ahead: +14 min · 15 mi”

16
00:01:42,335 --> 00:01:51,401
Play: simulated drive along the planned route (not GPS)

17
00:01:51,401 --> 00:01:58,568
Animation toggle: turn motion off for a calmer, reduced-motion view

18
00:01:58,896 --> 00:02:08,766
Free, keyless data: Open-Meteo forecasts · Valhalla/OSRM routing · SunCalc sun position
Manual demos use hand-set synthetic data. Planning aid, not a safety system. Built with Kiro.
